# DianaSh golden corpus. Recorded from the C# shell, byte for byte; EMUSEN_DIANASH_GOLDEN=record rewrites it - see EmuSen_DianaSh.md §13.4.
# Patterns: <ROOT> is the sandbox's real root, <TEMP> the corpus's real temporary folder, <INSTALL> the install's real directory;
# a 'match' block is a regular expression the whole output must match, written where a line prints a time or a measured number.
command coretop
usage 1   coretop [-w]                  live htop-style dashboard of the loaded core's hardware (Ctrl+C to exit - interactive terminal only;
usage 2                                 -w opens it in a separate window instead, if this frontend supports one)

case needs a terminal, and -w needs a window
target fake
covers 1-2
$ coretop
out 97
coretop: needs a real interactive terminal (stdin/stdout is redirected, or this console has none)
status 1
action none
$ echo $?
out 1
1
status 0
action none
$ coretop -w
out 46
coretop: -w is not supported by this frontend.
status 1
action none
$ echo $?
out 1
1
status 0
action none
$ coretop extra
out 97
coretop: needs a real interactive terminal (stdin/stdout is redirected, or this console has none)
status 1
action none
end

case with no target
target none
covers 1
$ coretop
out 58
No ROM loaded - this command needs an active debug target.
status 1
action none
$ echo $?
out 1
1
status 0
action none
end
